Motion polish (Liquid Glass only): adapted from Convx (https://github.com/cosmictaserdev-creator/Convx, GPL-3.0):
  - app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/ui/component/shimmer/ShimmerHost.kt (layer-isolated shimmer with bottom fade),
    from Convx ui/component/shimmer/ShimmerHost.kt
  - app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/ui/component/motion/GooeyTransition.kt (blur + alpha-threshold merge effect),
    from Convx ui/component/floatingtabbar/GooeyTransition.kt
  - app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/ui/component/motion/NavBarFold.kt and the folded navigation pill in
    ui/component/AppNavigation.kt, modelled on Convx FloatingTabBarScrollConnection / FoldingTabBar.
Playlist import by link (utils/PlaylistLinkImport.kt, viewmodels/PlaylistLinkImportViewModel.kt,
  ui/screens/settings/PlaylistLinkImportDialog.kt): Apple Music link parsing, title normalisation and the import flow
  adapted from Convx (https://github.com/cosmictaserdev-creator/Convx, GPL-3.0) canvas/AppleMusicPlaylist.kt,
  AppleMusicCatalog.kt and viewmodels/AppleMusicImportViewModel.kt.

Ambient mode and animated artwork (app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/ui/screens/ambient,
  app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/canvas, app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/ui/player/AnimatedArtwork.kt):
  adapted from Convx (https://github.com/cosmictaserdev-creator/Convx, GPL-3.0): AmbientModeScreen.kt,
  canvas/AppleMusicCatalog.kt, applecanvas/AppleMusicCanvasProvider.kt and ui/player/CanvasArtworkPlayer.kt.
  Motion artwork is looked up in Apple Music's public catalog; videos and artwork remain the property of their owners.

Spotify Canvas as animated covers (app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/spotify/SpotifyCanvas*.kt, used by canvas/AnimatedArtworkRepository.kt):
  the flow (track search, then the track's canvas on Pathfinder v2, query hashes read from the web player's scripts, the rules
  that decide which result is the same recording) is adapted from BitChord (https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord, GPL-3.0):
  data/canvas/SpotifyCanvas.kt, SpotifyCanvasQuery.kt, web/extension/lib/spotify.ts and TrackMatcher; rewritten for Auralys.
  Canvas videos remain the property of their owners.

Spotify account in the Library (app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/spotify, ui/screens/library/SpotifyLibraryScreen.kt and
  SpotifyPlaylistScreen.kt, ui/screens/settings/SpotifySettings.kt): the flow of signing in with the user's own Spotify session
  (sp_dc cookie), reading a web-player token from an offscreen web view, the Pathfinder GraphQL queries for playlists, a
  playlist's tracks and Liked Songs, the reading of the query hashes from the web player's scripts, and the pages that show the
  list at once and match its songs to YouTube Music in the background are adapted from BitChord
  (https://github.com/kushagrasinghx/BitChord, GPL-3.0): auth/SpotifyLoginScreen.kt, data/canvas/SpotifyToken.kt,
  data/spotify/SpotifyLibrary.kt, SpotifyImporter.kt, the Spotify library screen and web/docs/spotify-and-discord.md.
  Auralys re-implements the ideas; the sign-in cookie is kept in a private file that is left out of backups. Spotify's
  content and artwork remain the property of their owners; Auralys never plays Spotify audio.

Song poster cut-out (app/src/main/assets/poster/modnet_q.bin, code in app/src/main/kotlin/com/metrolist/music/poster/cutout):
  MODNet portrait matting (Zhanghan Ke et al., https://github.com/ZHKKKe/MODNet), Apache License 2.0,
  converted and compressed by Auralys; details and hashes in app/src/main/assets/licenses/NOTICE-poster.txt (also inside the APK assets).
